<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Two capabilities. There is no runtime API to read your own entitlements, and an unsigned
  simulator build carries none (`CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED[sdk=iphonesimulator*] = NO`, project.yml:26),
  so NEITHER is exercised by the gate; both are proven on a signed device build only.

  1. Sign in with Apple (Phase 4 Task 2). "Default" means a first-party Apple ID sign-in (the
     alternative, "Default WebCredentials", is for sharing an account system with a website —
     FitrahTube has none). The owner registered the App ID `com.albunyaan.tube` with this
     capability on 2026-09-20. The UI cannot read this file, so it reads the build-time flag
     FITRAH_APPLE_SIGNIN_REGISTERED instead, set in the untracked Config/Local.xcconfig
     (scripts/write-local-xcconfig.sh).

  2. Associated Domains: Universal Links for the app's own share URLs,
     https://app.fitrahtube.com/{watch,channel,playlist}/<id>, with or without a leading /api
     (`DeepLinkParser` routes both; `.onOpenURL` in FitrahTubeApp delivers them). The backend's
     AASA (`WellKnownController`) lists those six prefixes with Apple's `*`, which SPANS slashes;
     a deeper URL is captured too and `DeepLinkParser` then opens the app to nothing. The App ID
     needs this capability enabled in the portal as well, and links only fire once the AASA is
     served on app.fitrahtube.com; until then they open in Safari.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.developer.applesignin</key>
    <array>
        <string>Default</string>
    </array>
    <key>com.apple.developer.associated-domains</key>
    <array>
        <string>applinks:app.fitrahtube.com</string>
    </array>
</dict>
</plist>
